    {
      "id": "y089l37",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2.2.2 Rivers of Punjab"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hvtkbe1",
      "content": "Punjab's name comes from its five rivers. However, after the 1947 partition, three rivers (Jhelum, Chenab, Ravi) largely flow through Pakistan. Indian Punjab is irrigated mainly by the Beas and Sutlej."
    },
    {
      "id": "022kc7c",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>River</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Origin</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Length in Punjab</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Facts</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sutlej</p>",
            "<p>Mansarovar Lake, Tibet (Rakas Tal)</p>",
            "<p>~600 km in India</p>",
            "<p>Largest river of Punjab; enters Punjab at Ropar; joins Chenab in Pakistan</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Beas</p>",
            "<p>Beas Kund, near Rohtang Pass, Himachal Pradesh</p>",
            "<p>~290 km</p>",
            "<p>Joins Sutlej near Harike (Firozpur district); Harike Wetland/Bird Sanctuary here</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ravi</p>",
            "<p>Bara Bangahal, Chamba district, HP</p>",
            "<p>~80 km in Indian Punjab</p>",
            "<p>Flows along India-Pakistan border; Ravi-Beas waters part of Indus Waters Treaty</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Chenab</p>",
            "<p>Bara Lacha Pass, Himachal Pradesh</p>",
            "<p>Mostly in Pakistan</p>",
            "<p>Flows through J&amp;K; enters Pakistan; part of Indus Waters Treaty</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Jhelum</p>",
            "<p>Verinag spring, Kashmir Valley</p>",
            "<p>Mostly in J&amp;K/Pakistan</p>",
            "<p>Part of Indus Waters Treaty; assigned to Pakistan</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
