      "content": "2.6 Irrigation in Punjab"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Memorize Doabs and their bounding rivers: Bist Doab (Beas and Sutlej) and Bari Doab (Beas and Ravi).",
        "Remember Harike Wetland is located at the confluence of the Beas and Sutlej rivers and is a designated Ramsar site.",
        "Distinguish between physiographic zones: the Shivalik foothill region (Kandi) versus the central Alluvial Plains."
      ],
      "id": "ryd6iu4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u5c6zft",
      "content": "Punjab is one of the most irrigated states in India. Canal irrigation is the backbone of Punjab's agriculture. Key irrigation projects:"
    },
    {
      "id": "kbvws6n",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Project/Canal</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>River</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Significance</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bhakra-Nangal Dam</p>",
            "<p>Sutlej</p>",
            "<p>One of India's highest gravity dams (226m); Gobind Sagar reservoir; serves Punjab, Haryana, Rajasthan</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Beas Project (Pandoh Dam)</p>",
            "<p>Beas</p>",
            "<p>Diverts Beas waters to Sutlej via Pandoh-Sundernagar tunnel</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ranjit Sagar Dam (Thein Dam)</p>",
            "<p>Ravi</p>",
            "<p>Located in J&amp;K near Pathankot border; serves Punjab for irrigation and power</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Harike Barrage (Ferozepur)</p>",
            "<p>Beas-Sutlej confluence</p>",
            "<p>Feeds Bikaner Canal and Rajasthan Canal; Harike Wetland formed here</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sirhind Canal</p>",
            "<p>Sutlej (from Rupar headworks)</p>",
            "<p>Oldest major canal; irrigates Ludhiana, Patiala, Sangrur, Fatehgarh Sahib</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Upper Bari Doab Canal (UBDC)</p>",
            "<p>Ravi (from Madhopur headworks)</p>",
            "<p>Irrigates Gurdaspur, Amritsar, Tarn Taran</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>SYL Canal (Sutlej-Yamuna Link)</p>",
            "<p>Sutlej to Yamuna</p>",
            "<p>Proposed; highly contentious between Punjab and Haryana; not yet completed</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Indus Waters Treaty (1960)</p>",
            "<p>All Punjab rivers</p>",
            "<p>Treaty between India and Pakistan; eastern rivers (Beas, Ravi, Sutlej) to India; western rivers (Indus, Jhelum, Chenab) to Pakistan</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
